<title>USA: AT&amp;T, U S West go to arbitration over Iowa.</title>
<headline>AT&amp;T, U S West go to arbitration over Iowa.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES, Iowa 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>AT&amp;T Corp said arbitration proceedings between it and U S West Communications Group will begin Wednesday in an effort to bring local telephone service competition to Iowa.</p>
<p>During the arbitration, the Iowa Utilities Board will hear testimony from both companies and other potential new entrants.</p>
<p>Under the federal Telecommunications Act passed earlier this year, companies seeking to offer local service can ask state regulators to intervene and settle disputed or unresolved issues.</p>
<p>	   -- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
